<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
	Apple's privacy manifest for the app target.

	Capacitor and Cordova ship their own manifests inside their binary
	xcframeworks, and both are accurately empty. The seven Capacitor plugin SPM
	packages ship none and compile straight into this target, so their API use
	is declared here.

	Exactly one required-reason category applies, verified against the built
	Release binary rather than assumed: @capacitor/filesystem reads file
	creation and modification dates, because src/lib/native/journey-backup.ts
	keeps the durable journey mirror. Reason C617.1 is "files inside the app
	container", which is precisely and only what that mirror touches.
	The reinstall marker uses ordinary file existence and write operations in
	Application Support; it does not introduce a UserDefaults category.

	Deliberately NOT declared, each confirmed absent from the shipped binaries:
	DiskSpace, SystemBootTime, ActiveKeyboards, UserDefaults. The web bundle
	adds nothing — localStorage, IndexedDB and crypto.subtle are WebKit
	internals, not required-reason APIs.

	NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypes is empty because the shipping build is
	guest-only and nothing user-identifying leaves the device. Revisit this
	together with the App Store Connect privacy answers before account sync is
	enabled by default on native.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<key>NSPrivacyTracking</key>
	<false/>
	<key>NSPrivacyTrackingDomains</key>
	<array/>
	<key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypes</key>
	<array/>
	<key>NSPrivacyAccessedAPITypes</key>
	<array>
		<dict>
			<key>NSPrivacyAccessedAPIType</key>
			<string>NSPrivacyAccessedAPICategoryFileTimestamp</string>
			<key>NSPrivacyAccessedAPITypeReasons</key>
			<array>
				<string>C617.1</string>
			</array>
		</dict>
	</array>
</dict>
</plist>
